meta {
  name: Hold a slot (start checkout)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "practitionerId": "0198e3f0-3000-7000-8000-000000000010",
    "slotKey": "rule:0198e3f0-3000-7000-8000-000000000001:2026-10-05T08:00:00.000Z",
    "startsAt": "2026-10-05T08:00:00.000Z",
    "consultationType": "in_person",
    "offeringId": "0198e3f0-3000-7000-8000-000000000020",
    "locationId": null,
    "preferredLanguage": "fr"
  }
}

docs {
  Step 1 of the two-step booking: hold → confirm.

  Pick a slot from `GET /v1/practitioners/{id}/availability` and send back its `key`
  and `startsAt` verbatim (`slotKey` looks like `rule:<ruleId>:<isoStart>`,
  `exception:…` or `explicit:…`). `offeringId` is one of the practitioner's active
  offerings from the public profile (`offerings[]`); `locationId` may stay null when
  the slot already carries a location. `preferredLanguage` must be one the
  practitioner speaks.

  201 → a `held` appointment with `holdExpiresAt` (10 min by default). Confirm it with
  `POST /v1/appointments/{id}/confirm` before then, or the hold lapses and is reported
  as `expired`.

  To book for someone else add exactly one of `dependentId` (a managed dependent) or
  `subjectUserId` (a linked account holder); both together is a 422.

  Failure outcomes worth demoing:
  - 409 `SLOT_UNAVAILABLE` — another patient holds/booked that time, or your calendar view
    was stale (the slot is re-derived from the live schedule).
  - 409 `PROFILE_INCOMPLETE` — booking for yourself needs a completed patient profile.
  - 409 `BOOKING_LIMIT_REACHED` — one account may hold/confirm at most 10 upcoming
    appointments at a time (`APPOINTMENT_MAX_LIVE_PER_BOOKER`).
  - Re-sending the same hold (same slot, same subject) returns the SAME appointment —
    its `holdExpiresAt` is never extended. Bookings open 60 days ahead (422 beyond).
  - 403 `NOT_A_CAREGIVER` — on-behalf booking without an active caregiver link.
  - 422 — offering/location/language don't match the practitioner or consultation type.

  For a zero-config end-to-end run, use flows/booking instead of this catalog file.
}
